// What a lazy build still owes the library. A name the program takes is a name
// bin/idc loads the library's function for, so a collision of names, of
// exports or of structs is found among functions the build holds. What no name
// betrays is a body: a function the program wrote that does what an idstd one
// does, without calling it. These checks compare the program's bodies against
// the index of the ones that were not loaded, and are the only ones that need
// it; a type error in an unloaded function is not one.

ext_check() {
  if(len((import ext_n)) > 0) {
    ext_uniq_pass();
    ext_imd_pass();
  }
} return void;
